   "title": "My Family (2)",
   "en": "There are four people in my family, and each of them has a special way of making our home feel safe and bright. Every Saturday morning we clean the house together, and my job is to wipe the table while my brother makes the beds badly and laughs about it. Last winter I had a high fever at night, and my mother sat by my bed with a wet towel, changing it again and again until the morning light came. The next morning I got up a little earlier and did it again by myself. We are not a rich family, and our holidays are simple, but my parents always find a way to make a small trip feel like a great adventure. My mother gets up before the sun and fills the kitchen with the smell of porridge, eggs and warm milk, and she never once complains about being tired. One afternoon I sat still for ten minutes and simply watched, and I noticed three things I had walked past a hundred times. At that moment I felt warm and a little shy, and I did not know where to put my hands. I learned that being brave does not mean you are not afraid; it means you go on even when you are. So now, whenever the same chance comes again, I will not wait so long before I say yes.",
   "zh": "我家有四口人，他们每个人都有特别的办法，让家里既安全又明亮。每周六早上我们一起打扫，我擦桌子，弟弟铺床铺得歪歪扭扭，还笑个不停。去年冬天我夜里发高烧，妈妈坐在床边用湿毛巾一遍遍给我敷额头，一直到天亮。第二天早上我起得早了一点，自己又做了一遍。我家并不富裕，假期也简单，可爸妈总有办法让一次小小的出游变成一场大冒险。妈妈天不亮就起床，把厨房弄得满是粥、鸡蛋和热牛奶的香味，她从不抱怨累。有一天下午我坐着不动看了十分钟，发现了三样走过一百次都没注意的东西。那一刻我又暖又有点不好意思，不知道手该往哪儿放。我学到了：勇敢不是不害怕，而是害怕的时候仍然往前走。所以下次同样的机会来时，我不会再犹豫那么久才答应。",
