   "title": "My Family (13)",
   "en": "My family is small but full of warmth, and every evening our little flat turns into the busiest and happiest place I know. My little brother follows me everywhere like a small shadow, and although he sometimes annoys me, I would not trade him for anything. Every Saturday morning we clean the house together, and my job is to wipe the table while my brother makes the beds badly and laughs about it. I had to try twice before I got it right, and the second time felt easy. Last winter I had a high fever at night, and my mother sat by my bed with a wet towel, changing it again and again until the morning light came. We are not a rich family, and our holidays are simple, but my parents always find a way to make a small trip feel like a great adventure. One afternoon I sat still for ten minutes and simply watched, and I noticed three things I had walked past a hundred times. At that moment I felt warm and a little shy, and I did not know where to put my hands. I learned that being brave does not mean you are not afraid; it means you go on even when you are. So now, whenever the same chance comes again, I will not wait so long before I say yes.",
   "zh": "我家不大，却充满温暖；每天傍晚，我们的小房子就变成我认识的最热闹、最快乐的地方。弟弟像个小影子一样跟着我，虽然有时很烦人，可我拿什么也不换他。每周六早上我们一起打扫，我擦桌子，弟弟铺床铺得歪歪扭扭，还笑个不停。我试了两次才做对，第二次就觉得轻松了。去年冬天我夜里发高烧，妈妈坐在床边用湿毛巾一遍遍给我敷额头，一直到天亮。我家并不富裕，假期也简单，可爸妈总有办法让一次小小的出游变成一场大冒险。有一天下午我坐着不动看了十分钟，发现了三样走过一百次都没注意的东西。那一刻我又暖又有点不好意思，不知道手该往哪儿放。我学到了：勇敢不是不害怕，而是害怕的时候仍然往前走。所以下次同样的机会来时，我不会再犹豫那么久才答应。",
