   "title": "A Sunny Day (54)",
   "en": "I like watching the sky before it rains, because the clouds gather slowly like a big grey family meeting above the roofs. I love the ten minutes after a heavy rain, when the clouds break and the sun makes every puddle shine like a small mirror. Last week the rain was so heavy that the road turned into a river, and my father carried me across on his back. The next morning I got up a little earlier and did it again by myself. Weather is not good or bad; it is only different, and the same rain that ruins a picnic makes the garden green. When the first drops hit the dusty ground, the whole street smells of wet earth, and everybody stops to breathe it in. One afternoon I sat still for ten minutes and simply watched, and I noticed three things I had walked past a hundred times. At that moment I felt warm and a little shy, and I did not know where to put my hands. I learned that being brave does not mean you are not afraid; it means you go on even when you are. So now, whenever the same chance comes again, I will not wait so long before I say yes.",
   "zh": "我喜欢看雨前的天空，云慢慢聚拢，像一大片灰色的家庭会议开在屋顶上。我喜欢大雨后的十分钟，云裂开，太阳把每个水洼照得像小镜子。上周雨大得路变成了河，爸爸把我背了过去。第二天早上我起得早了一点，自己又做了一遍。天气没有好坏，只是不同；同一场雨毁了野餐，却让花园变绿。第一滴雨落在积灰的地上，整条街都是湿土的味道，人人都停下来深吸一口。有一天下午我坐着不动看了十分钟，发现了三样走过一百次都没注意的东西。那一刻我又暖又有点不好意思，不知道手该往哪儿放。我学到了：勇敢不是不害怕，而是害怕的时候仍然往前走。所以下次同样的机会来时，我不会再犹豫那么久才答应。",
