   "title": "A Rainy Day (73)",
   "en": "The weather changes the colour of my street, the sound of my steps and even the way I feel in the morning. On very hot days the road shines like water, and the trees stand still as if they were too tired to move. In summer my mother puts a bowl of water on the balcony for the birds, and by noon it is always half empty. I did not finish everything, but I finished more than I expected. Last week the rain was so heavy that the road turned into a river, and my father carried me across on his back. Weather is not good or bad; it is only different, and the same rain that ruins a picnic makes the garden green. One afternoon I sat still for ten minutes and simply watched, and I noticed three things I had walked past a hundred times. At that moment I felt warm and a little shy, and I did not know where to put my hands. I learned that being brave does not mean you are not afraid; it means you go on even when you are. So now, whenever the same chance comes again, I will not wait so long before I say yes.",
   "zh": "天气会改变我这条街的颜色、我脚步声的响动，甚至我早上的心情。特别热的时候路面亮得像水，树一动不动，像累得挪不动。夏天妈妈在阳台放一碗水给鸟喝，到中午总是少了一半。我没有把所有事都做完，但做完的比预想的多。上周雨大得路变成了河，爸爸把我背了过去。天气没有好坏，只是不同；同一场雨毁了野餐，却让花园变绿。有一天下午我坐着不动看了十分钟，发现了三样走过一百次都没注意的东西。那一刻我又暖又有点不好意思，不知道手该往哪儿放。我学到了：勇敢不是不害怕，而是害怕的时候仍然往前走。所以下次同样的机会来时，我不会再犹豫那么久才答应。",
