   "title": "Healthy Fruits (104)",
   "en": "Every city has a smell that belongs only to it, and in my city that smell is hot oil, spring onions and fresh bread. In summer we eat cold noodles with cucumber and vinegar, and the whole family makes a happy noise while eating. Once I tried to cook noodles alone and put in three times too much salt, and we ended up eating bread for dinner. My teacher wrote one short sentence on my notebook and smiled at me. Cooking is not difficult; it only asks you to pay attention, and paying attention is a useful habit everywhere. At the market the vegetable sellers call out their prices, and my mother walks slowly, touching every tomato before choosing. One afternoon I sat still for ten minutes and simply watched, and I noticed three things I had walked past a hundred times. At that moment I felt warm and a little shy, and I did not know where to put my hands. I learned that being brave does not mean you are not afraid; it means you go on even when you are. So now, whenever the same chance comes again, I will not wait so long before I say yes.",
   "zh": "每座城市都有只属于它的味道，我这座城市的味道是热油、葱和新面包。夏天我们吃黄瓜醋凉面，全家吃得心满意足、响声不断。有一次我自己煮面，盐放了整整三倍，结果我们晚饭吃的是面包。老师在我的本子上写了一句短短的话，还朝我笑了笑。做饭不难，它只要求你用心，而用心在任何地方都是好习惯。菜市场里摊主吆喝着价钱，妈妈慢慢走，每个番茄都要摸一摸才挑。有一天下午我坐着不动看了十分钟，发现了三样走过一百次都没注意的东西。那一刻我又暖又有点不好意思，不知道手该往哪儿放。我学到了：勇敢不是不害怕，而是害怕的时候仍然往前走。所以下次同样的机会来时，我不会再犹豫那么久才答应。",
