   "title": "My Favorite Sport (221)",
   "en": "I am not the strongest or the fastest in my class, but sport has taught me things that marks cannot measure. Jumping rope looks easy until you try to do it for two minutes without stopping. The last five minutes of a match are the most honest, because nobody has the energy to pretend anymore. I had to try twice before I got it right, and the second time felt easy. Last year our class lost every match, and yet we still trained every Tuesday, which I am now proud of. When I look back now, I think the best part was simply being there. Sport teaches you to lose in front of people, which is a lesson that life repeats later anyway. One afternoon I sat still for ten minutes and simply watched, and I noticed three things I had walked past a hundred times. At that moment I felt warm and a little shy, and I did not know where to put my hands. I learned that being brave does not mean you are not afraid; it means you go on even when you are. So now, whenever the same chance comes again, I will not wait so long before I say yes.",
   "zh": "我不是班里最强壮或最快的，可运动教会了我分数衡量不了的东西。跳绳看着简单，直到你试着一口气跳两分钟。比赛最后五分钟最真实，因为谁都没力气再装了。我试了两次才做对，第二次就觉得轻松了。去年我们班每场都输，可每周二仍然训练，现在我很为此骄傲。现在回想起来，我觉得最好的部分就是当时在场。运动教你在众人面前输，这一课生活以后反正还会重复。有一天下午我坐着不动看了十分钟，发现了三样走过一百次都没注意的东西。那一刻我又暖又有点不好意思，不知道手该往哪儿放。我学到了：勇敢不是不害怕，而是害怕的时候仍然往前走。所以下次同样的机会来时，我不会再犹豫那么久才答应。",
