   "title": "A Competition of Lying",
   "titleZh": "",
   "en": "A certain old gentleman was very unhappy, about modern education, and thought that young people didn't know the difference between right and wrong. One day he was taking a walk near the church when he saw some young boys standing around a small cat. The old gentlemen went up to the boys and asked them what was happening. One of the boys said to him: \"We're having a competition. \" We're telling lies, and the one who tells the biggest lie will keep the cat. The old gentleman thought this was a good, chance to teach the boys a useful lesson, so he said to them, \"I've never told a lie in my life\". At, once there was a great shout from all the boys, and they said, \"You've won! The cat belongs to you!\"",
   "zh": "某个老年绅士对现代教育颇为不满，他认为年轻人不知道是非之间的差异。有一天，他在教堂附近散步时，看到一些小男孩围着一只小猫。这位老绅士凑上前去问孩子们发生什么事了。有个男孩告诉他：我们正在进行一场竞赛。我们在比赛说谎，谁说的谎最大，这只猫就是谁的。老绅士觉得这是教育孩子们的一个好机会。于是他就对孩子们说：“我这辈子从未说过谎话。”立刻所有孩子异口同声地大喊：“你赢了！这只猫属于你了",
